al-Nutritional Prioritizing Tool is a method used to assess nutritional needs in patients, particularly those with liver disease.", "FUNCTIONAL ASSESSMENT IN LIVER TRANSPLANTATION STUDY:This study evaluates muscle function, mass, and quality in candidates for liver transplantation, providing insights into their nutritional status.", "DUAL-ENERGY X-RAY ABSORPTIOMETRY:Dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry is a technique used to measure bone density and body composition, including muscle mass in patients with liver cirrhosis.", "COMPUTED TOMOGRAPHY:Computed tomography is an imaging technique used to assess muscle mass and other anatomical features in patients with liver cirrhosis.", "ALCOHOLIC HEPATITIS:Alcoholic hepatitis is a liver condition caused by excessive alcohol consumption, often leading to malnutrition and cirrhosis.", "PRIMARY BILIARY CIRRHOSIS:Primary biliary cirrhosis is a chronic disease that slowly destroys the bile ducts in the liver, leading to cirrhosis and nutritional issues.", "MUSCLE ATROPHY:Muscle atrophy is the loss of muscle mass that can occur in patients with cirrhosis. This condition is often associated with poor nutritional status, highlighting the importance of adequate nutrition in maintaining muscle health.", "PHASE ANGLE:Phase angle is a measure derived from bioelectrical impedance analysis that can indicate nutritional status and cellular health in patients with cirrhosis.", "NUTRITIONAL ASPECTS OF CHRONIC LIVER DISEASE:This refers to the various dietary and nutritional considerations that are important for managing chronic liver disease."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}